# Arcen Pier: keep the shared X11 and ICE socket directories out of the
# daily /tmp clean-up.
#
# systemd creates /tmp/.X11-unix and /tmp/.ICE-unix root-owned 1777 only at
# boot (x11.conf, "D!"), and its daily `systemd-tmpfiles --clean` ignores
# boot-only entries, so it ages them like any other /tmp directory. A host
# that ran no desktop for ten days loses them, and the next desktop's
# compositor recreates them as its own user, which locks every other user's
# GNOME Shell out of X11. These lines only exclude them from ageing; the
# boot entries still create and empty them.
x /tmp/.X11-unix
x /tmp/.ICE-unix
